    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d220">

                <pb facs="0383" n="1841" xml:id="pg1841"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">794A.5 MAP/10–3151: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the Republic of China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Rankin</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Taipei</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-10-31T15:00:00+08:00">October 31, 1951—3
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>563. Complying Deptel 351, Oct 24, re budget
                    control I have sent note to FonOff<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d220-f1"/> covering points mentioned in first full para reftel and in third full para mytel 504, Oct
                    17</p>
                <p>Also propose address letter to FonMin
                    requesting he convey my appreciation to Generalissimo for his attention and
                    support in instituting new arrangements, also incorporating in letter substance
                    para Deptel 351. FonMin will reply by letter confirming he has conveyed my msg to
                    Generalissimo and latter familiar with and giving support to new
                        arrangements.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d220-f2"/> This is for the record.</p>
                <p>Further propose to review subject with Generalissimo when I take new ECA mission chief Schenck<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d220-f3"/> to call on him soon after latter’s arrival about 12 days
                    hence.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rankin</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d220-f1" n="1" xml:id="d220-f1-content">
                <p>The text of the note, dated October 30, 1951, not printed, was sent to the
                    Department as an enclosure to despatch 204, November 13, 1951
                    (893.10/11–1351).</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d220-f2" n="2" xml:id="d220-f2-content">
                <p>Rankin’s letter to Foreign Minister Yeh, dated November 5, 1951, and Yen’s reply
                    of November 6, neither printed, were sent to the Department as enclosures to the
                    despatch cited in footnote 1, above.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d220-f3" n="3" xml:id="d220-f3-content">
                <p>Hubert G. Schenck was replacing Moyer as head of the ECA Mission.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
